WEBVTT

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:09.640
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, all. Everyone survive the weekend? My grand plans for the garden lasted about ten minutes before the rain arrived.</v>

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:15.099
<v David Whitfield>Ten minutes? You did better than us. Didn't even get the chairs out.</v>

00:00:17.539 --> 00:00:26.640
<v Hannah Price>I'd settle for the heating in the portakabin making its mind up. Coat on, coat off, all morning. Just having a moan, not reporting a job.</v>

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:30.879
<v Marcus Hale>That's the deluxe climate control. Two settings, both wrong.</v>

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:38.560
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes the weather forecast. Monday the ninth, morning stand-up. What's already closed out?</v>

00:00:39.789 --> 00:00:44.689
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, I tested the air dryer yesterday and it's all fine now. That's finished.</v>

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:50.490
<v Priya Raman>That's the air dryer test done, then? Nothing outstanding from that?</v>

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:53.780
<v Grace Liu>Correct. Done and dusted.</v>

00:00:54.829 --> 00:01:03.229
<v David Whitfield>And I signed off the inspection on the 11kV Switchboard on Tuesday. That's old news, really, but it was still coming up in conversation.</v>

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.629
<v Sarah Okafor>Last Tuesday, yeah? We're talking completed work.</v>

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:11.540
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, last Tuesday. Signed off, not another inspection for today.</v>

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:18.689
<v Grace Liu>One observation as well: noticed the water ring was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down.</v>

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:23.959
<v Marcus Hale>Settled back down, yeah. Not something we're opening work on from that.</v>

00:01:24.799 --> 00:01:27.250
<v Grace Liu>Exactly. Just passing on what I saw.</v>

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:37.109
<v Priya Raman>And I heard a slight rattle from the big valve by the gate, nothing to action yet. Before that turns into a strip-down on someone's list.</v>

00:01:38.159 --> 00:01:40.959
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. The rattle itself isn't a new job.</v>

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.790
<v Priya Raman>Yep, just an observation at this point.</v>

00:01:46.849 --> 00:01:54.200
<v Grace Liu>Separate from that noise, I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the big valve by the gate by 11am.</v>

00:01:55.810 --> 00:02:01.760
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Grace Liu. Permit to work and isolation for the big valve by the gate, by 11am.</v>

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.450
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, that's mine. By 11am.</v>

00:02:07.019 --> 00:02:12.270
<v David Whitfield>Just keeping the distinction clear—permit and isolation, not me being volunteered to chase the rattle?</v>

00:02:14.479 --> 00:02:16.930
<v Grace Liu>Exactly. No extra investigation being added there.</v>

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:21.409
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. What have we got that's still blocked?</v>

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:29.870
<v Marcus Hale>I can't get to the palletizer until production gives us a window. Still stuck on that, I'm afraid.</v>

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:35.770
<v Fiona Doyle>There's no window confirmed. So it's not a commitment we can put into today.</v>

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:39.710
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine, stays blocked. We're not pretending that's going ahead.</v>

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:44.530
<v Priya Raman>Um, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the CT1 either.</v>

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:48.560
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, no confirmed delivery date. Nothing firm to plan against.</v>

00:02:49.479 --> 00:02:52.629
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Blocker noted, no assumption that it's arriving today.</v>

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.340
<v Hannah Price>A delivery date would be a lovely novelty, wouldn't it?</v>

00:02:59.169 --> 00:03:08.270
<v Sarah Okafor>And we were going to replace the belt on the trucks but that's been pushed to next month, so ignore it. Cancelled out of today's work.</v>

00:03:09.419 --> 00:03:12.219
<v David Whitfield>One less ghost job following us round, then.</v>

00:03:13.189 --> 00:03:15.639
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Not quietly putting it back in.</v>

00:03:16.509 --> 00:03:21.759
<v Marcus Hale>On the admin bit, I'll sort the training records for the new starters by Thursday.</v>

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:27.520
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Marcus. Training records for the new starters, by Thursday.</v>

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:33.340
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, I'll take that. Thursday, not claiming they're finished already.</v>

00:03:34.919 --> 00:03:39.120
<v Hannah Price>That's the records themselves you're talking about, rather than extra training sessions?</v>

00:03:39.659 --> 00:03:42.460
<v Marcus Hale>The records, yeah. That's the job I'm taking.</v>

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:44.710
<v Fiona Doyle>Got you. By Thursday.</v>

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:50.800
<v Priya Raman>And I'll run a function test on the dryer. No rush on that one.</v>

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:56.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Pri has the function test on the dryer. No rush.</v>

00:03:57.169 --> 00:04:02.069
<v Priya Raman>Yeah. And that's separate from the air dryer test we were just talking about.</v>

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:06.870
<v Grace Liu>Yep—my air dryer test is finished. We're not reopening that.</v>

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:12.110
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, talked over you there. Heard 'dryer' twice and thought Teams had started looping.</v>

00:04:12.949 --> 00:04:19.250
<v Priya Raman>No, just us being us. I'll do the function test on the dryer, no rush, no deadline added.</v>

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:30.189
<v Fiona Doyle>There's also a site visit at Kestrel with the contractor that needs doing. Not an emergency but don't let it slip. It hasn't got anyone against it.</v>

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:35.860
<v Sarah Okafor>Is anyone able to take that site visit at Kestrel with the contractor?</v>

00:04:38.199 --> 00:04:39.949
<v David Whitfield>I can't take it on.</v>

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:43.990
<v Priya Raman>I can't commit to that either, sorry.</v>

00:04:45.509 --> 00:04:47.959
<v Marcus Hale>No, not one I can pick up.</v>

00:04:50.079 --> 00:04:54.279
<v Fiona Doyle>Still nobody, then. I'm raising the gap, not volunteering for the visit.</v>

00:04:55.730 --> 00:05:02.029
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. We agree it needs doing, but Kestrel stays unallocated. Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:05:04.319 --> 00:05:13.769
<v Hannah Price>Other gap: the sensors on the GT2 water valve need recalibrating this afternoon. It matters but it's not urgent. Nobody's got that as far as I know.</v>

00:05:15.449 --> 00:05:21.050
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, did you say this afternoon, but not urgent? Just making sure I've heard both bits.</v>

00:05:21.959 --> 00:05:30.009
<v Hannah Price>Yeah. Recalibrate the sensors on the GT2 water valve this afternoon. It matters but it's not urgent. I'm flagging it, not taking it.</v>

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:32.720
<v Sarah Okafor>Any taker for that recalibration?</v>

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:38.540
<v Priya Raman>I can't put my name to it. Don't want my question sounding like an offer.</v>

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:40.379
<v David Whitfield>Nor me, I'm afraid.</v>

00:05:40.699 --> 00:05:49.449
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that's unowned as well. The sensors on the GT2 water valve need recalibrating this afternoon; it matters but it's not urgent. No owner agreed.</v>

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:59.029
<v Fiona Doyle>Agreed. Both that and the site visit at Kestrel with the contractor remain unallocated. Not putting either against someone by default.</v>

00:06:00.009 --> 00:06:06.660
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. For the three things people have taken, just give me a quick yes on what you've committed to.</v>

00:06:08.279 --> 00:06:14.579
<v Grace Liu>Yep. I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the big valve by the gate by 11am.</v>

00:06:16.579 --> 00:06:20.430
<v Marcus Hale>I'll sort the training records for the new starters by Thursday.</v>

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:25.339
<v Priya Raman>And I'll run a function test on the dryer. No rush.</v>

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:28.810
<v Hannah Price>Lovely. And my portakabin moan remains strictly a moan.</v>

00:06:29.189 --> 00:06:33.740
<v Sarah Okafor>Duly recorded as British conversation, not maintenance. Thanks, everyone. We'll leave it there.</v>
